WEBVTT

00:07.070 --> 00:08.220
That's...

00:08.860 --> 00:10.440
a frost spider!

00:10.870 --> 00:12.420
Neema, come here.

00:15.250 --> 00:18.410
<i>I can sense it...
It's feeling starved and panicked.</i>

00:18.830 --> 00:21.230
<i>I can tell that it's hungry.</i>

00:21.230 --> 00:24.380
<i>But why is it panicky?</i>

00:28.530 --> 00:29.390
Neema!

00:29.840 --> 00:31.590
You mustn't interfere.

00:32.110 --> 00:34.050
This is his battle.

01:08.350 --> 01:09.420
Look out!

01:14.810 --> 01:16.100
Wow!

01:16.100 --> 01:18.960
<i>Even though he's a huge
 hobgoblin capable of speech,</i>

01:18.960 --> 01:21.530
<i>to the frost spider, he's just food.</i>

01:21.840 --> 01:22.760
<i>This is...</i>

01:25.560 --> 01:29.710
<i>This is a hardcore life-or-death 
battle for survival!</i>

01:38.820 --> 01:43.700
<b><i>Fluffy Paradise</i></b>

03:00.450 --> 03:04.950
<b><i>Episode 6   The Desire to Become Stronger</i></b>

03:29.680 --> 03:32.860
<i>If he actually loses here,</i>

03:33.140 --> 03:37.070
<i>Papa will probably incinerate them
without a second thought.</i>

03:38.320 --> 03:41.400
<i>It's so that we humans can survive...</i>

03:42.550 --> 03:47.500
<i>I get that. It's just another form 
of the survival of the fittest.</i>

03:47.500 --> 03:48.250
<i>But...</i>

04:18.240 --> 04:22.850
I managed to avoid being crushed 
because of that ultimate cheat

04:22.850 --> 04:24.810
or whatever you put on me.

04:24.810 --> 04:26.070
Thank you.

04:31.870 --> 04:33.050
<i>There it is again.</i>

04:35.940 --> 04:38.760
<i>I'm getting a very strong sense of panic.</i>

04:39.860 --> 04:41.740
<i>What's making you feel that way...?</i>

04:45.770 --> 04:47.920
<i>Help... me...</i>

04:48.950 --> 04:50.130
<i>You need help?</i>

04:50.400 --> 04:53.850
<i>Want to... protect my child...</i>

04:54.250 --> 04:57.310
<i>Your child? You have a child?</i>

05:02.880 --> 05:05.870
<i>I see. It's because she was pregnant.</i>

05:06.670 --> 05:09.480
<i>That's why she was so panicked.</i>

05:10.110 --> 05:12.850
<i>She needed to eat lots and lots,</i>

05:12.850 --> 05:16.380
<i>but the ecosystem has been messed up
since the goblins arrived.</i>

05:18.520 --> 05:20.520
<i>She couldn't catch any food...</i>

05:22.310 --> 05:24.340
<i>She's a victim too.</i>

05:24.780 --> 05:25.900
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

05:26.400 --> 05:30.500
<i>I don't like God,
but let me pray just this once.</i>

05:34.760 --> 05:39.540
<i>If she goes to the afterlife 
and maybe another life after...</i>

05:39.880 --> 05:43.980
<i>Please let her live in peace.</i>

05:45.610 --> 05:46.440
Neema...

05:50.180 --> 05:51.790
I know.

05:55.670 --> 05:59.370
No matter the situation, 
only the strongest will survive.

05:59.370 --> 06:04.140
I can't change that just 
because I want to be selfish.

06:09.070 --> 06:11.790
<i>If it was possible to save her, 
I really wish I could have.</i>

06:12.610 --> 06:16.250
<i>But I didn't.</i>

06:16.250 --> 06:19.730
<i>I was too scared of the 
responsibility of saving her.</i>

06:25.690 --> 06:27.560
<i>I want to become stronger...</i>

06:27.560 --> 06:32.750
<i>So that every living creature can 
live happily where they belong.</i>

06:32.750 --> 06:36.380
<i>It doesn't matter how. I just 
want to be able to help them.</i>

06:43.820 --> 06:45.870
Have you calmed down a bit?

06:46.310 --> 06:47.100
Yeah.

06:55.430 --> 06:57.210
The hobgoblin...

07:18.340 --> 07:20.670
<i>Wh-Who might you be?!</i>

07:20.670 --> 07:21.950
He must've evolved.

07:21.960 --> 07:23.920
<b>Evolved?</b>

07:22.370 --> 07:23.920
Evolved?

07:24.440 --> 07:26.510
Are you the hobgoblin?

07:26.510 --> 07:29.230
Yeah. What happened?

07:29.670 --> 07:31.630
<i>I'd like to know that myself!</i>

07:31.630 --> 07:34.050
<i>I guess even he has no idea.</i>

07:36.530 --> 07:37.680
<i>I know!</i>

07:37.680 --> 07:39.600
<i>I can always count on Sol!</i>

07:39.870 --> 07:44.820
<i>Sol! It looks like the hobgoblin 
may have evolved or something?</i>

07:45.150 --> 07:46.480
Evolved?

07:46.480 --> 07:49.370
The highest order of goblin species
is the hobgoblin,

07:49.370 --> 07:51.280
so it cannot evolve any further.

07:51.660 --> 07:53.240
<i>Say what now?!</i>

07:53.240 --> 07:55.740
<i>But, but he sorta looks human now!</i>

07:55.740 --> 07:57.360
<i>And he's got some horns.</i>

07:57.610 --> 07:58.980
Horns?

07:58.980 --> 08:05.830
I do know that the oni who live in Wazhite
 possess human bodies and horns.

08:06.150 --> 08:07.230
<i>Oni?!</i>

08:07.230 --> 08:09.150
<i>I'd like to see him for myself.</i>

08:09.150 --> 08:11.720
<i>At long last, I shall visit you
 in person tomorrow.</i>

08:12.840 --> 08:14.530
What did the great dragon say?

08:14.990 --> 08:17.730
He wants to see for himself, 
so he'll come tomorrow.

08:18.560 --> 08:20.420
Hmm...

08:21.560 --> 08:25.870
<i>I mean, I guess he looks like an oni, but he 
seems much flashier than the Japanese ones.</i>

08:26.960 --> 08:29.110
G-Get the hobgoblin some clothes!

08:40.780 --> 08:41.990
Lemme see!

08:42.830 --> 08:43.570
There.

08:44.250 --> 08:45.470
Oh!

08:47.910 --> 08:50.540
Thank you so much for saving us!

08:52.540 --> 08:54.900
Neema! It's time for little girls
 to be in bed!

08:54.900 --> 08:56.760
More importantly, get away from him!

08:56.760 --> 08:59.180
Get away from him this instant! No! Bad!

09:06.300 --> 09:09.400
What would you like to do?
Wanna come with me?

09:09.400 --> 09:12.560
Or would you like to stay in this 
forest where your mommy lived?

09:15.030 --> 09:16.900
<i>I wonder if it isn't sure...</i>

09:21.810 --> 09:23.620
Aw, so cute!

09:23.620 --> 09:25.840
Your name's going to be Gratia.

09:25.840 --> 09:29.020
Your lovely mother made me stronger
 and protected you,

09:29.020 --> 09:31.320
and <i>gratia</i> is what I want to tell her.

09:31.320 --> 09:33.580
It means "thank you."

09:33.580 --> 09:36.060
It's nice to meet you, Gratia.

09:41.040 --> 09:43.220
H-Huh?

09:43.660 --> 09:48.360
<i>Did I do something I wasn't
 supposed to again...?</i>

09:56.910 --> 09:58.880
That feels much better!

10:00.970 --> 10:03.340
Start loading up the parts that are ready.

10:04.240 --> 10:08.830
We'll be reusing her carapace, 
so make sure you handle it with care.

10:08.830 --> 10:11.240
You there. Mind her venomous fangs.

10:11.240 --> 10:12.230
Hey, hey!

10:13.410 --> 10:16.360
Will you free the human adults now, too?

10:16.360 --> 10:17.460
Yeah, sure.

10:17.810 --> 10:18.750
Really?

10:19.110 --> 10:22.960
Well, if we're going along with 
your plan, they'd be a burden.

10:23.320 --> 10:25.130
Thanks!

10:25.460 --> 10:27.650
Neema! Morning.

10:27.650 --> 10:30.040
Good morning, Nino and Pino.

10:30.040 --> 10:31.380
Good morning...

10:41.350 --> 10:43.780
Don't worry about it.

10:49.370 --> 10:51.850
We can eat breakfast over there.

10:53.650 --> 10:55.600
Nino, let's go eat.

10:56.030 --> 10:57.050
Yeah!

10:58.430 --> 11:00.200
<i>They're like angels.</i>

11:01.230 --> 11:02.410
My lady.

11:03.110 --> 11:04.840
This little one's all better now.

11:06.750 --> 11:08.380
Thank you!

11:08.380 --> 11:09.130
No problem.

11:09.780 --> 11:13.220
<i>Amazing! His healing magic worked perfectly!</i>

11:13.220 --> 11:15.070
So fluffy!

11:15.730 --> 11:17.900
Father, this little one...

11:18.370 --> 11:23.330
Neema, you're smart, so you know how 
much responsibility owning a pet is.

11:24.470 --> 11:25.910
Of course I do!

11:26.190 --> 11:31.240
I think it's best for it
to stay where it belongs.

11:31.700 --> 11:33.810
Does that mean I can't keep it?

11:35.440 --> 11:39.390
When wild animals are kept by humans, 
it distorts their disposition.

11:39.390 --> 11:43.240
They might lose their guard or become
unable to find food on their own.

11:44.440 --> 11:48.090
Think of the distortion as ripples on water.

11:48.090 --> 11:49.260
Ripples?

11:49.520 --> 11:51.800
If you take that rabbit home with you,

11:51.800 --> 11:54.070
it will form a small ripple in the world.

11:54.720 --> 11:59.270
That ripple will continue on forever,
 bumping into other ripples

11:59.270 --> 12:01.880
and swallowing them or getting swallowed up.

12:02.630 --> 12:04.900
It will affect the world.

12:05.480 --> 12:08.450
Every single day, countless ripples form.

12:08.450 --> 12:11.230
All such phenomena shape this world.

12:12.330 --> 12:15.270
It doesn't matter how big or small they are.

12:15.270 --> 12:18.740
They all impact the world in some fashion.

12:21.050 --> 12:25.430
And someday, they end up coming back to us.

12:25.820 --> 12:28.990
So the fewer ripples in the world, the better.

12:28.990 --> 12:33.900
When there are no ripples, that means
 the world is at peace. Understand?

12:37.580 --> 12:41.330
No matter what, you will be the
 center of a ripple, Neema.

12:41.680 --> 12:43.630
So it's best to be cautious, okay?

12:45.240 --> 12:49.580
<i>How rude! I'm content just being 
able to pet and fluff all the floofs.</i>

12:49.950 --> 12:51.960
<i>I mean, if someone got in my way,</i>

12:51.960 --> 12:55.870
<i>I'd take advantage of Papa's authority 
or Sol's cheaty magic to destroy them.</i>

12:57.200 --> 12:59.800
<i>Wait. Is that the kind 
of thinking that's wrong?</i>

13:01.600 --> 13:03.130
Oh well.

13:03.610 --> 13:07.080
I'm sorry we hurt you. 
Let's play again sometime.

13:11.190 --> 13:13.780
<i>Aw, I'm so lonely...</i>

13:17.550 --> 13:18.980
<i>That's right.</i>

13:18.980 --> 13:24.640
<i>I have Nox with me, Dee waiting at home, 
and I'll be able to see Sol later.</i>

13:27.480 --> 13:28.350
What's wrong?

13:29.080 --> 13:33.330
Father, you see... 
Well, there's this little one.

13:36.840 --> 13:39.990
Neema! That's not even an 
animal! It's a monster!

13:40.370 --> 13:43.350
Furthermore, the fact that it's 
black means it's one of a kind!

13:43.350 --> 13:46.840
<i>Oh, right. The color black 
isn't very good in his world.</i>

13:47.190 --> 13:49.790
Do you know the difference 
between an animal and monster?

13:50.300 --> 13:53.120
It's whether they have their own
thoughts or not, right?

13:53.120 --> 13:55.760
<i>That's right. Mister Dan mentioned before</i>

13:55.760 --> 13:59.720
<i>that animals and monsters are separated
by how well they can think.</i>

14:00.510 --> 14:03.270
Is that how humans see it?

14:04.630 --> 14:09.310
In short, monsters are failures.
They're defective.

14:10.030 --> 14:11.740
Defective?

14:11.740 --> 14:15.810
Yes. Goblins are defective 
versions of humans.

14:16.250 --> 14:19.090
Frost spiders are defective spiders.

14:19.490 --> 14:21.610
That's why most monsters are weak.

14:23.340 --> 14:27.040
In order for one to get stronger, 
it must be given a name.

14:27.040 --> 14:30.510
That frost spider probably also had a name.

14:30.850 --> 14:32.230
A name?

14:32.490 --> 14:34.860
If you're given a name by someone powerful,

14:34.860 --> 14:37.340
the world recognizes you as an individual.

14:37.700 --> 14:42.220
Then you can use magic
 and receive blessings from spirits.

14:42.570 --> 14:44.270
<i>Huh... I see.</i>

14:44.540 --> 14:48.700
<i>There's also the True Name Vow... 
Names must be really important in this world.</i>

14:49.000 --> 14:51.250
So what's your name?

14:51.250 --> 14:53.650
<i>It must be pretty impressive!</i>

14:54.470 --> 14:55.360
I don't have one.

14:55.830 --> 14:58.790
What?! When you're <i>that</i> strong?!

14:59.570 --> 15:02.120
Honestly, I'm jealous of this one.

15:03.670 --> 15:07.340
It has a mark on its forehead, 
meaning it's been named.

15:08.300 --> 15:10.450
Her name is Gratia!

15:11.830 --> 15:12.710
Neema!

15:12.710 --> 15:14.710
I didn't mean to do anything bad!

15:15.460 --> 15:18.690
Then so be it.
I guess we're taking her with us.

15:20.610 --> 15:22.560
Isn't that great?

15:23.940 --> 15:26.990
Your Grace, we're all set.

15:26.990 --> 15:27.930
Good.

15:33.860 --> 15:35.920
All right, let's go.

15:35.920 --> 15:39.580
<i>After that, because the former
 hobgoblin was leaving,</i>

15:39.860 --> 15:43.420
<i>I had Sol cast a protective 
spell on the cave.</i>

15:45.050 --> 15:50.530
<i>The hobgoblin took extra care to
tell the goblins not to go outside</i>

15:50.530 --> 15:53.810
<i>because we wouldn't be able 
to help if anything happened.</i>

15:56.770 --> 16:01.030
<i>With everything that happened,
our party grew bigger than when we started...</i>

16:01.030 --> 16:06.280
<i>But it's all happily ever after, and we're
 returning to the village at long last!</i>

16:13.060 --> 16:16.870
Thank goodness. What house do you two live in?

16:16.870 --> 16:19.580
We actually live in the Ireiga Proxy nearby.

16:21.130 --> 16:24.280
Wait, are you two Earl Ireiga's children?

16:24.510 --> 16:25.360
Yes.

16:25.360 --> 16:27.740
Ireiga is our family name.

16:28.510 --> 16:32.300
I see. Then we'll have to make sure 
you're escorted safely.

16:35.180 --> 16:37.680
I'll also send a messenger pigeon,

16:37.680 --> 16:40.140
but you should head home as soon as possible.

16:40.490 --> 16:41.180
Yes, sir.

16:41.560 --> 16:44.150
Pino, Nino, be careful.

16:44.150 --> 16:45.740
We will. Thank you.

16:47.480 --> 16:48.240
Nino?

16:50.530 --> 16:52.910
<i>D-Does she hate me?! Why?!</i>

16:53.460 --> 16:56.870
You sure about this? You're the one
 who'll regret it later, Nino.

16:59.450 --> 17:02.000
Why don't you... sometime?

17:02.500 --> 17:05.470
Come again? Do what sometime?

17:10.090 --> 17:12.850
Hey, what are you doing, Pino?!

17:13.290 --> 17:15.820
It's because you're being difficult, Nino!

17:19.960 --> 17:23.140
I-I said, why don't you...

17:27.620 --> 17:30.770
come to our house sometime?
You can come over and play.

17:33.760 --> 17:37.440
Wh-What? Y-You don't have to
 come over if you don't want to!

17:39.910 --> 17:41.150
What a tsundere.

17:41.520 --> 17:42.380
Huh?

17:46.470 --> 17:50.010
Yeah, I'll definitely come by to play.

17:52.700 --> 17:56.450
Hey! What are you doing?! Get off of me!

17:56.450 --> 17:57.820
Nope!

17:57.820 --> 17:59.210
I said get off!

17:59.210 --> 18:01.060
Nope, nope, nope, nope!

18:01.060 --> 18:02.330
Hey!

18:10.150 --> 18:13.930
<i>He's so perfectly smooth!
Sol's scales are the best!</i>

18:15.190 --> 18:18.020
He's different from any oni I've ever seen.

18:18.020 --> 18:20.370
There are also remnants of elemental power.

18:20.370 --> 18:23.080
<i>I wonder if I can nap with Sol today.</i>

18:23.080 --> 18:25.850
<i>Will I go for the classic
using his tummy as a pillow,</i>

18:25.850 --> 18:28.920
<i>or should I use his wing as a blanket?</i>

18:28.920 --> 18:30.010
Are you listening, child?

18:30.010 --> 18:31.840
Hmm. Decisions, decisions...

18:32.120 --> 18:34.670
Heed me, Neema!

18:38.440 --> 18:42.230
<i>H-He startled me! And called me by my name!</i>

18:44.240 --> 18:45.150
Thanks!

18:45.650 --> 18:50.590
This one is not an oni.
Oni cannot use elemental powers.

18:51.490 --> 18:53.440
Elemental powers?

18:53.440 --> 18:56.110
<i>That's what the holy beasts use, right?</i>

18:56.110 --> 18:57.950
Can you see spirits or anything?

18:58.450 --> 19:02.910
If these translucent bug-looking
 creatures count, then yes.

19:03.300 --> 19:04.370
Bugs?

19:04.620 --> 19:06.950
Then can you use elemental powers?

19:07.390 --> 19:08.890
Maybe if I knew how.

19:09.560 --> 19:11.340
I shall show you.

19:13.960 --> 19:17.310
Let's see... What would make a good target?

19:17.310 --> 19:18.220
My lady.

19:27.650 --> 19:31.010
Here is a clay doll created 
with earth magic. Will this work?

19:31.010 --> 19:32.640
Yay! Thank you!

19:34.130 --> 19:36.600
Here's your target! Give it a try!

19:36.990 --> 19:39.070
Defeat that clay doll.

19:44.170 --> 19:49.180
W-Wow... It completely fell apart.

19:49.180 --> 19:53.790
Fire elemental power?
And you can conjure it remotely?

19:54.140 --> 19:59.510
All he said to the fire spirit was,
"Defeat that clay doll."

19:59.940 --> 20:02.200
Can you do other elements as well?

20:03.440 --> 20:04.170
<i>In the end...</i>

20:05.790 --> 20:07.640
<i>He was able to use wind,</i>

20:09.600 --> 20:11.110
<i>water,</i>

20:13.400 --> 20:15.310
<b>sparkly</b>

20:13.400 --> 20:15.310
<b>Somehow
made him</b>

20:13.480 --> 20:15.320
<i>and earth too!</i>

20:15.320 --> 20:19.010
<i>He was able to use them all!
Talk about cheating.</i>

20:19.320 --> 20:23.950
Elemental powers, huh?
They might prove useful in that one plan.

20:23.950 --> 20:26.460
Huh? That one plan?

20:27.540 --> 20:30.340
<i>I haven't told Papa about it yet!</i>

20:31.160 --> 20:36.130
Um... I figured out a way for humans 
and monsters to live peacefully together.

20:36.130 --> 20:39.170
I would like for you to help me out, Father.

20:39.170 --> 20:41.590
I'll tell you the details later, okay?

20:42.040 --> 20:43.830
All right, sure.

20:46.050 --> 20:47.560
More importantly...

20:47.810 --> 20:50.770
You're a new creature now!

20:51.170 --> 20:55.180
Let's see... How about Shinki?

20:55.720 --> 20:57.160
Shinki?

20:57.470 --> 20:59.850
<i>Written with the kanji
for "forest" and "oni"!</i>

20:59.850 --> 21:02.130
<i>I am so awesome at naming things.</i>

21:11.000 --> 21:12.330
Neema...

21:12.330 --> 21:13.730
Y-You've got it all wrong!

21:13.730 --> 21:16.700
That's not <i>his</i> name! It's his species!

21:17.010 --> 21:20.640
So this is how you keep gaining
 more servants to serve you.

21:20.640 --> 21:21.790
Nuh-uh!

21:22.100 --> 21:26.510
<i>Damn that God! He's definitely enjoying this!</i>

21:26.790 --> 21:29.880
Sorry for giving you a name without asking.

21:30.280 --> 21:33.510
It's all right. I was going to ask you anyway.

21:33.510 --> 21:33.980
Huh?

21:34.310 --> 21:37.540
Because you're the one who showed us the way.

21:41.720 --> 21:46.060
The goblins led by me, Shinki,
will all swear fealty to you, Nefertima.

21:46.780 --> 21:51.480
And because you gave me my name,
you are my master.

21:54.740 --> 21:57.140
<i>I-Is this okay?</i>

21:57.660 --> 21:58.510
<i>Either way...</i>

22:00.570 --> 22:03.160
It's good to have you, Shinki.

23:35.180 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.180 --> 23:40.010
<b>I Believe I Can Be of Some Service</b>
